course: dictionary
lesson: 2724
title: Words for church life
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A diocese is a large area that holds many churches. «Bishops are senior leaders who look after many churches in an area called a diocese.» The clue is in the word many: a diocese is more than one church, and a bishop looks after all of them.
explain: Try the swap test. Replace diocese with «area» in the sentence: «Bishops are senior leaders who look after many churches in an area.» It still makes sense, so an area is close to what a diocese means. Diocese is simply the church name for that kind of area.
explain: Diocese can also mean the church community and the offices that run the area. Words ending in -an, like diocesan, usually describe something that belongs to a diocese. A diocesan school is a school linked to that church area.
fact: A diocese is an area with many churches, looked after by a bishop.
fact: A bishop is a senior church leader who looks after a diocese.
fact: The bishop's main church in a diocese is called the cathedral.
fact: «Diocesan» describes something that belongs to a diocese, such as a diocesan school.
fact: Phrases you may meet are «the Diocese of…» and «bishop of the diocese».
exercise: «Bishops are senior leaders who look after many churches in an area called a diocese.» What is a diocese? | *An area with many churches, looked after by a bishop | A type of hat worn by church leaders | A kind of church building | A short service held on Sundays
exercise: Find and copy the word that names the senior leader of a diocese. | *bishop | dioceses | cathedral | pilgrim
exercise: A school linked to a church area is called a diocesan school. What does diocesan describe? | Something that is always closed | Something that is very old | Something only for adults | *Something that belongs to a diocese
test: In a diocese, what is the bishop's main church called? | A village hall | A chapel | *The cathedral | A monastery
test: Which phrase names a church area? | A diocesan cake sale | The diocese is a kind of food | Diocese time for a cup of tea | *The Diocese of Oxford
exam: Mrs Patel says «the Diocese of York» is a school. Is she right? | Yes, because the bishop teaches all the lessons | Yes, it is always a school | No, it is a kind of sports team | *No, it is an area of churches looked after by a bishop
